---

import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";
import { getAboutHeroPhoto } from "../../lib/aboutPhotos";

const page = getAboutPage("kit-qr-onboarding")!;
const hero = getAboutHeroPhoto(page.slug);
---
<AboutArticle
  slug={page.slug}
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  heroImage={hero?.image}
  heroAlt={hero?.alt}
  heroCaption={hero?.caption}
  heroCredit={hero?.credit}
  heroCreditHref={hero?.sourceUrl}
>
  <h2>Guided kit path</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Buy an ESP32 + waterproof DS18B20.      <a class="text-link" href="/about/esp32-freeze-kit">parts list</a>
      (Adafruit / Amazon; ThermalTrace does not sell hardware).
    </li>
    <li>Create a push device on <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/devices">Dashboard → Devices</a> (one click: named Workshop probe by default).</li>
    <li>Copy or scan the ingest QR (visible for 30 minutes after create/rotate).</li>
    <li>Flash firmware or point Home Assistant at that URL: sensors auto-import on first POST.</li>
    <li>Set freeze °F + email on the inline first-alert card on Devices, or open <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/alerts?tab=settings#alert-section-essentials">Alerts → Essentials</a>, then send a test.</li>
    <li>Optional: <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/share/links">Share a family live link</a> (included on Free).</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What to encode</h2>
  <p>
    After creating or rotating a push key on <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/devices">Dashboard → Devices</a>,
    the key callout shows a QR for the full ingest URL (visible for 30 minutes, survives refresh):
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`https://your-domain/api/ingest/YOUR_DEVICE_KEY`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Anyone scanning the QR on a phone sees the URL, keep devices physically secure; rotate keys if a sticker is lost.
  </p>

  <h2>NFC tags (optional)</h2>
  <p>
    Write the same HTTPS ingest URL as an NDEF URI record on an NTAG213/215 sticker. Phones can tap to open the URL
    during setup. Keep tags with the kit — they are as sensitive as a printed QR.
    Parts and print tips:
    <a class="text-link" href="/kit-labels">Kit QR &amp; NFC labels</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>QR on the Devices page</h2>
  <p>
    The QR is generated in-app when you create or rotate a push key, no external QR generators required.
    You can download the SVG or print a simple label (device name + QR + URL) from that callout.
    See also the curl test payload in
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/ingest-and-webhooks">Ingest & webhooks</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Onboarding checklist</h2>
  <p>
    Prefer to see readings before flashing firmware?
    Use <strong>Try without hardware</strong> on Overview for the demo pull feed, browse the public <a class="text-link" href="/demo">live demo</a>, then create a push device and scan the QR.
  </p>
  <p>
    The dashboard getting-started card tracks device creation, first POST, and alerts.
    Sensor keys auto-import when firmware POSTs JSON: pair the QR with payload keys like <code>temp1</code>, <code>door1</code>, then rename labels on Devices if needed.
  </p>
</AboutArticle>
